    "",
    "Text S1. Sample pretreatment and SPE method for quantification of antibiotics",
    "Filtered samples（200ml）were acidified with hydrochloric acid to pH 3. 0.2 g Na2EDTA chelating agent and internal standard (50 ng for each sample) were added to samples. HLB cartridges (500 mg, 6 mL, Waters) were firstly activated with 10 mL methanol (MS grade), 10 mL ultra-pure water and 10 mL acid (pH=3); Leachate samples were add to cartridges at a flow rate of 2 mL/min, then rinse the cartridges with 20 mL HCl (pH=3) to remove the salts; After that, cartridges were dried with a stream of N2 and eluted with 1 mL of methanol and kept at 4 ℃ in dark until tested. ",
    "",
    "Text S2. Analysis of the antibiotics",
    "For analysis of the antibiotics, 18 target compounds were quantified by the external standard method, and the correlation coefficients (r²) of calibration curves for all the target antibiotics were typically above 0.99. Mass spectrometry conditions: ESI positive/negative ion mode, curtain gas of 35 psi, ionization voltage was 5500V-4500V, desolventizing temperature was 500 ℃, atomizing gas of 55 psi, auxiliary heating gas of 55 psi, multiple reaction monitoring (MRM) was used to analyze the sample. Liquid chromatography conditions: methanol solvent, column was ACQUITY BEH C18 2.1*100 mm 1.7 um, temperature was 40 ℃, mobile phase A was 0.1% formic acid + pure water, mobile phase B was 0.1% formic acid + acetonitrile. ",
    "Table S1. The physicochemical properties of target antibiotics in this study.",
